---
/* Component — Page
 * The page canvas: sets the base background and the document text colour
 * together, so a consumer gets a legible canvas that theme-flips via the
 * semantic dark overrides. It is also the sticky-footer host: a full-viewport-
 * height flex column so its header/main/footer children stack top-to-bottom and
 * the footer is held at the viewport bottom even when the content is short (see
 * PageMain). align-items stays at the default stretch, so the full-width header
 * and footer bands still bleed edge to edge.
 *
 * Renders <body> itself. The consumer's page owns <html> and <head>, and keeps
 * setting data-theme/dir and loading the named fonts — the system declares
 * family stacks only. */
---

<body>
  <slot />
</body>

<style>
  body {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    margin: 0;
    min-block-size: 100dvh;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    background: var(--bravoixr-color-surface-page);
    color: var(--bravoixr-color-text);

    /* The page's base typography, inherited by everything that has no rule of
     * its own. The canvas owns both halves: surface and text colour above, and
     * the type they are read in below. Components that need different type
     * declare it; everything else inherits from here, which is why the library
     * needs no separate base-text rule. */
    font-family: var(--bravoixr-font-body);
    font-size: var(--bravoixr-text-body);
    font-weight: var(--bravoixr-weight-body);
    line-height: var(--bravoixr-leading-prose);
    letter-spacing: var(--bravoixr-tracking-prose);
  }

  /* Propagate border-box to everything on the canvas — box-sizing doesn't
   * inherit on its own, so descendants inherit it explicitly. This gives the
   * page a global box model without the system shipping a separate universal
   * reset. :global() is required here: slotted content is rendered by the
   * consumer, so it never carries this component's scope attribute and a plain
   * descendant selector would not reach it. The rule stays bounded to the page
   * subtree regardless.
   *
   * Note Astro leaves `html`/`body` selectors unscoped by design, so the rule
   * above emits as a plain `body { … }` rather than a scoped selector. */
  body :global(*),
  body :global(*)::before,
  body :global(*)::after {
    box-sizing: inherit;
  }
</style>
